PURPOSE Build the paper arc model and initial vehicle/package route pools.
INPUT network, InputDataset, variant and optional inherited branch restrictions
OUTPUT model with vehicle/package Y, service indicators, status and a feasible Plan
REFERENCES public vrp_time_space.cs; Program calls to the two absent initializers
PAPER Eqs. 5-17; network rule catalog; periodic rescheduling framework

PROCEDURE BuildArcModel(network,input,variant,node=none)
    REQUIRE all model inputs use one identified catalog and cost convention
    create binary Y[k,a] for every physical-vehicle arc
    create binary Y[r,a] for every complete-package-layer arc
    minimize etaK * sum(k,a) c[k,a]*Y[k,a]
           + etaR * sum(r,a) c[r,a]*Y[r,a]
    include pi[r] through the package unserved arc cost, once per order
    FOR each physical vehicle k
        add total super-source outflow - inflow = 1                 [6]
        add total super-sink inflow - outflow = 1                   [7]
        add internal incoming = outgoing at every other vertex     [8]
        add sum(a) duration[k,a]*Y[k,a] <= dutyLimit[k]              [14]
    FOR each order r
        add total source outflow - inflow = 1                      [9]
        add total sink inflow - outflow = 1                        [10]
        add incoming = outgoing at every transfer state/time       [11]
        add incoming = outgoing at all other internal states       [12]
        if stored as r+/r-, match their transfer location/time exactly
    FOR each vehicle k and order r
        S[k,r] := sum of k's selected service-indicator arcs for r
            using the transfer/service incidence definition in Eq. 13
        REQUIRE S[k,r] has the declared 0/1 service-event interpretation
        expose S as assignment metadata Z, not an independent free assignment
    FOR each k and supported state transition s in A_phi
        packageUse[r,s] := sum of compatible package arc variables for r
        vehicleUse[k,s] := sum of compatible physical vehicle arc variables
        add sum(r) packageUse[r,s]*S[k,r] <= Cp[k]*vehicleUse[k,s]    [13]
        if a linear model is requested, create U[k,r,s] in [0,1]:
            U <= packageUse; U <= S; U >= packageUse+S-1
            use sum(r) U[k,r,s] <= Cp[k]*vehicleUse[k,s]
    use only families 3..10,14,15 for the supported subset           [17]
    require ordered connected paths; impose cycle elimination if needed
    apply declared LT schedule restrictions, availability and service eligibility
    IF variant == dynamic
        apply input.dynamicState commitments through FreezeLegacyDecisions
    IF node exists
        impose all inherited vehicle/package decisions on the corresponding Y
        use the same stable keys and required values as pool filtering/pricing
    return model with network,input,configuration,variable maps and row metadata

PROCEDURE SolveArcModel(model,limits=model.configuration.limits)
    optimize under limits; record solver status, incumbent availability and bound
    IF no incumbent: return ArcResult with plan=none and unavailable values
    check integer tolerance; extract ordered vehicle and complete package paths
    reconstruct carrier assignments with no carrier changes outside legal transfers
    plan := Plan(paths,assignments,acceptedOrders,unservedOrders,cost,modelId,input)
    IF ValidatePlan(plan,model.input,model.configuration) fails
        return status=invalid_candidate,plan=none with diagnostic records
    return ArcResult{incumbent:true,objective,solverBound,status,
                     arcMaps:Y,assignments:Z,plan,scope:declared_arc_model}

PROCEDURE CreateSeedPool(network,input,node=none)
    pool := empty RoutePool; initialSolutions := empty records; alternateResults := []
    FOR each physical vehicle k
        enumerate every legal unused connector as a complete vehicle route
        also retain any required committed continuation supplied by the prior plan
        for each route satisfying node restrictions: MergeColumn(pool,route)
    FOR each order r
        if unserved is permitted and compatible with node/commitments
            for every legal unserved connector/time copy
                MergeColumn(pool,complete package route with cost pi[r])
    initial := SolveArcModel(BuildArcModel(network,input,initial,node),
                             input.configuration.limits.initialization)
    IF initial.plan exists
        merge ExtractSplitColumns(initial,initializationKind=initial)
    FOR each order r missing a physical-service seed, within the seed budget
        model := BuildArcModel(network,input,virtual_package,node)
        prohibit r's unserved arc; allow other uncommitted orders to be unserved
        alternate := SolveArcModel(model,input.configuration.limits.initialization)
        if alternate.plan exists
            merge ExtractSplitColumns(alternate,initializationKind=virtual_package)
        append alternate status and extracted route IDs to alternateResults
    CheckViews(pool)
    initialSolutions := {initial,virtual_package:alternateResults,
                         feasiblePlan:best validated complete plan or none}
    return pool,initialSolutions

ASSUMPTIONS
    CreateSeedPool uses constrained arc solves and enumerated fallback routes.
    This seed strategy is a design choice; the paper does not prescribe it.
    "virtual_package" names the seed-generation call. Unserved routes provide
    penalized coverage and do not represent physical service.
    A feasible seed pool may serve no orders. Branches and commitments can remove
    fallback choices; a failed seed solve returns its status.
    Service-indicator indexing, source/sink aggregation and carrier reconstruction
    use the declared catalog mapping.

IMPLEMENTATION
    Program.cs calls vrp_time_space_ini and vrp_time_space_vis_pas. Their initial
    route-pool interfaces are specified here; the class files are not distributed.
